  "title": "KDP: Validate option length to prevent infinite loop",
  "description": "Summary:\n\nIn dissect_kdp(), option_len was read from the packet without verifying that it is at least 2 bytes. When dissecting option 6 or unknown options, the dissector updates offset by (option_len - 2). If option_len is 0, this subtraction cancels out the preceding offset increments, causing an infinite loop in the options while loop and passing negative lengths to proto_tree_add_item().\n\nChanges:\n\n\\- Added a validation check breaking out of the options loop if option_len \\< 2.\n\n\\- Verified with tools/check_apis.py (0 warnings) and tools/check_typed_item_calls.py (0 warnings).",
