      "title": "KDP: Validate option length to prevent infinite loop",
      "message": "KDP: Validate option length to prevent infinite loop\n\n\nIn dissect_kdp(), option_len was read from the packet without verifying that it is at least 2 bytes. For option 6 and unknown options, the dissector updates offset with (option_len - 2). If option_len is 0, the subtraction cancels the previous increments, preventing offset from advancing and triggering an infinite loop or dissector exception.\n\nBreak out of the options loop if option_len is less than 2.",
